  "verified": "Groningen’s dated Ocasys programme record identifies the English-taught Campus Fryslân BSc Global Responsibility and Leadership, ISAT 59327, 180 EC. Its scheme has 50 EC named year-one foundations and methods, 15 EC named second-year leadership, ethics and statistics, a 10 EC Living Lab, a 30 EC minor and a 10 EC thesis with portfolio. Statistics I precedes Statistics II and Living Lab follows year-one foundations and methods and the second-year first-semester courses. Its entry text requires all foundation and skills lab courses. The Capstone runs in the final semester and awards 10 EC for thesis plus portfolio. No second thesis or credit-bearing portfolio is counted.",
  "officialAlternative": "Compared the official 2026-entry counsellor guide, 2025–2026 brochure, 2026–2027 Ocasys named courses and scheme, current public GPS programme page, November 5 renaming announcement and historical 2021–2022 TER. The latter has 15 EC per track and 25 EC of other post-propaedeutic electives, and is historical corroboration only. The dated scheme contains 13 unnamed 5 EC elective slots across three years and names six 5 EC courses under Energy, Ecology and Climate, split across two tracks with one cross-listed course. Its separate Optional Electives specialisation is hidden in the public catalogue. The current promotional page describes Planet and Politics instead of three GRL majors. No public rule located in this execution establishes which electives may fill all 13 slots for the September 2026 cohort or which transition applies. Forward-year scheme requests returned 403. The cited 115 EC is a verified subset, not a discrepancy in the degree’s 180 EC total.",
  "essentialEvidence": "Verify the elective allocation and progression rules for September 2026 entrants to the Energy, Ecology and Climate major, including which slots may draw outside its two tracks and whether the later Planet/Politics structure applies to this cohort.",
